---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Keep in sync with privacy/it.astro and with the server setup it describes
// (Traefik access log filter + logrotate, Remark42 compose in /srv/remark42).
const updated = '7 November 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What data this site collects, why, and for how long.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {updated} · <a href="/privacy/it/" hreflang="it" lang="it">Italiano</a></p>

    <p>
      This is a personal blog. It has no analytics, no ads, no tracking and no cookie banner, because there is
      nothing to consent to. The only personal data it handles is listed below.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Paolo Bietolini, <a href="mailto:privacy@paolobietolini.com">privacy@paolobietolini.com</a>. Write to this
      address for any question or request about your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site and the comments run on my own server at Infomaniak in Switzerland. Switzerland is recognised by
      the EU as providing an adequate level of data protection.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading the blog</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No cookies.</strong> If you use the light/dark switch, your choice is saved in your browser's
        local storage. It never leaves your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs record only failed requests</strong> (pages not found, blocked or failed requests):
        IP address, time, requested address and browser identifier. Successful page views are not logged.
        These logs are kept for <strong>7 days</strong> to detect abuse and fix errors, then deleted
        (legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
      </li>
      <li>
        The comments section loads from <code>comments.paolobietolini.com</code>, which is the same server.
        No third-party service is contacted while you read.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Comments</h2>
    <p>
      Comments use <a href="https://remark42.com">Remark42</a>, self-hosted on the server above. Commenting is
      optional. When you comment, this is stored:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the name you choose, your comment, the page and the time;</li>
      <li>
        a scrambled (hashed) version of your IP address, used only to fight spam and abuse. The original address
        is not stored;
      </li>
      <li>
        if you sign in with email: your email address, linked to your account. It is used to send you a one-time
        login code and is never shown publicly.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Login emails</strong> are sent through <a href="https://mailbox.org/en/data-protection-privacy-policy">mailbox.org</a>
      (Heinlein Hosting GmbH, Germany), my email provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Profile pictures:</strong> when you sign in with email, the comments server asks
      <a href="https://automattic.com/privacy/">Gravatar</a> (Automattic Inc., USA) whether a picture exists for a
      scrambled (hashed) form of your email address. If none exists, a generated picture is used. Your browser
      does not contact Gravatar; the request comes from my server.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Cookies:</strong> only after you sign in, <code>comments.paolobietolini.com</code> sets two cookies
      (<code>JWT</code> and <code>XSRF-TOKEN</code>) that keep you logged in and protect the form. They are strictly
      necessary for the login you asked for. The comments widget may also keep display settings, such as sort
      order, in your browser's local storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Legal basis:</strong> your request to publish a comment (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). Spam protection relies on
      legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)).
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>How long:</strong> comments stay as long as they are published. You can ask me to delete your
      comments or your whole account at any time. Backups of the comments database are kept for
      <strong>7 days</strong>, so deleted data disappears from backups within a week.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask for a copy of your data, its correction or deletion, and you can object to or restrict its
      processing. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@paolobietolini.com">privacy@paolobietolini.com</a> and I'll reply within
      30 days. You also have the right to complain to a data protection authority.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
